From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:41:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 306/311] avcodec: add V4L2 Request API AVS1 and AVS+ hwaccel

A hwaccel for the cavs decoder on the stateless AVS uAPI of the Allwinner
H616 cedrus driver: V4L2_PIX_FMT_AVS_FRAME, one coded picture (its
header and all its slices, both fields of a field coded picture) per
OUTPUT buffer, and the SEQUENCE, PICTURE and WEIGHT_QUANT controls, the
latter only for AVS+ pictures with weighting_quant_flag. The engine
parses the slice headers and removes the annex A pseudo start codes
itself, so the bitstream goes in as found and data_offset points at the
first slice start code (4, just after the picture start code, for the
pre-final revision streams without slice start codes).

References are the two most recent I or P pictures: FORWARD and
SECOND_FORWARD for I and P pictures, FORWARD (DPB[1]) and BACKWARD
(DPB[0]) for B pictures, where SECOND_FORWARD carries the distance and
flags of the reference before them for the direct mode of field coded
pictures. Each reference is described by its capture timestamp,
picture_distance, picture_structure, top_field_first and whether it was
intra coded. The uAPI definitions are carried in v4l2-stateless-avs.h
until the kernel headers have them.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
